From 752ffca625a94a234202e09e5292cad95f669ea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:42:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/26] software_isp: GPU detail stage, full-size GPU output

Add a light denoise and sharpening stage to the GPU debayer shaders: a
same-colour high-pass of the raw sample (centre minus the mean of its
four neighbours at distance 2) is removed below a noise threshold
(coring) and amplified above twice the threshold (unsharp mask), equally
on R, G and B. The strengths and the threshold come in DebayerParams; the
CPU debayer ignores them.

A new simple IPA algorithm, Detail, sets them from piecewise linear
curves over the analogue gain in the tuning file (sharpen, denoise,
threshold), so that noisy high-gain frames are smoothed more and
sharpened less.

The GPU debayer samples with GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE and scales its input, so
its output needs no border: allow output sizes up to the input size. A
1920x1080 stream then comes from a 1920x1080 sensor mode rather than from
the next larger one.

Signed-off-by: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
